meta {
  name: Stop enforcing
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

delete {
  url: {{groupService}}/roster
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "key": "{{groupKey}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("reports whether there was a roster to stop enforcing", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.cleared).to.be.a("boolean");
  });
}

docs {
  # Stop enforcing

  Drops the group's roster, so nothing is closed under that prefix again until one is stated.

  A group with no roster is one this service does not know the membership of, and it is left alone.
  A group whose roster is empty is a voice channel nobody is in, and everything on it is closed.
  The two look alike and mean opposite things, which is why stopping is its own request rather than an empty list.
}
